<p><br></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"641422a810c9" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292098ExecutiveSu=
mmary"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc2302=
92098"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292098"></span><=
/span>Executive Summary</h1>
<p>This Business Requirements Document (BRD) defines the combined capabilit=
y of customer-facing Landing Pages and the internal Customer App Landing Pa=
ge Settings module, enabling a fully controlled, secure, and business-manag=
ed digital experience.</p>
<p>The customer-facing Landing Pages provide a structured, end-to-end self-=
service journey for customers to securely access their case information, un=
derstand their enforcement stage, and complete key actions such as making p=
ayments or seeking support. These pages are personalised post-authenticatio=
n and are designed to drive clarity, reduce confusion, and increase success=
ful digital engagement and payment conversion while maintaining compliance =
and accessibility standards.</p>
<p>Complementing this experience, the Customer App Landing Page Settings mo=
dule enables authorised business users to manage and control the content di=
splayed on these Landing Pages without requiring technical intervention. Th=
rough this capability, users can access structured content areas aligned to=
 Landing Page sections (such as Payment, Enforcement, and Support), edit co=
ntent in a format that reflects the end-user view, apply formatting, insert=
 variables, and manage hyperlinks, while preserving the overall layout and =
structure of the pages.</p>
<p>All content changes are governed by a structured approval workflow compr=
ising Author, Reviewer, and Publisher roles, ensuring that updates are vali=
dated for accuracy, compliance, and policy alignment before being released =
to production. The system enforces segregation of duties, maintains a compl=
ete audit trail, and supports traceability through logged actions and times=
tamps at each stage of the approval process.</p>
<p>This combined solution ensures:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>A consistent and compliant customer experience across all Landing Pages<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Business-led control over content and messaging</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reduced dependency on development teams for content updates</p></li>
<li>
<p>Full auditability and governance of all changes</p></li>
<li>
<p>Alignment between backend case data, frontend presentation, and controll=
ed content evolution</p></li>
</ul>
<p>The BRD provides a comprehensive definition of functional behaviour, gov=
ernance rules, workflows, and system requirements necessary to deliver and =
manage both the customer journey and the supporting content management capa=
bility effectively.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"098c31b586bb" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292099BusinessObj=
ectives"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc23=
0292099"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292099"></span=
></span>Business Objectives</h1>
<p>The primary objective of this initiative is to deliver a controlled, sca=
lable, and business-managed digital capability that enables both an effecti=
ve customer self-service journey and a governed content management framewor=
k through the Customer App.</p>
<p><strong>Customer-Facing Objectives</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Enable customers to securely access and view their case information thro=
ugh Landing Pages following successful authentication</p></li>
<li>
<p>Provide clear, structured, and personalised information to help customer=
s understand their enforcement stage, outstanding balance, and next steps</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Drive increased self-service adoption and reduce dependency on agent-ass=
isted interactions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Improve payment conversion by guiding users toward the primary action us=
ing clear messaging and structured page design</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reduce disputes and confusion by presenting enforcement information in a=
 simplified and understandable format</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure all customer-facing content remains compliant, transparent, and a=
ccessible</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Business and Operational Objectives</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Enable business users to manage Landing Page content directly through th=
e Customer App without requiring technical intervention</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure all updates to Landing Page content, messaging, and journey eleme=
nts are controlled through a structured approval process</p></li>
<li>
<p>Maintain consistency across all customer-facing touchpoints by centralis=
ing content management</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reduce operational overhead and turnaround time for content updates by r=
emoving dependency on development cycles</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Governance and Compliance Objectives</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Enforce a three-step governance model (Author =E2=86=92 Reviewer =E2=86=
=92 Publisher) for all content changes</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure segregation of duties across all stages of the content update lif=
ecycle</p></li>
<li>
<p>Maintain a complete and traceable audit trail of all changes, approvals,=
 and publishing actions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure all published content is reviewed and approved for accuracy, comp=
liance, and policy alignment before being made live</p></li>
<li>
<p>Support audit, compliance review, and regulatory requirements through sy=
stematic tracking and logging</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Technology and Process Objectives</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Provide an intuitive content editing interface within the Customer App t=
hat reflects the structure and layout of the Landing Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>Allow business users to format content, insert variables, and configure =
hyperlinks while preserving page structure</p></li>
<li>
<p>Integrate with existing ticketing systems to manage approval workflows a=
nd track change requests</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure reliable and secure publication of approved content directly to p=
roduction environments</p></li>
</ul>
<p>These objectives collectively ensure that the solution delivers a high-q=
uality customer experience while maintaining strong governance, operational=
 efficiency, and compliance control.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"4fcebaa3bea3" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292100Scope"><spa=
n class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292100"><spa=
n class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292100"></span></span>Scope=
</h1>
<p></p>
<p><strong>In Scope</strong></p>
<p>The scope of this capability includes both the <strong>customer-facing L=
anding Pages</strong> and the <strong>Customer App Landing Page Settings mo=
dule</strong>, along with all associated content management, governance, an=
d supporting functionality.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Customer-Facing Landing Pages</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Sign-In / ID&amp;V Entry Page</p></li>
<li>
<p>Home / Timeline Page (Primary Landing Page)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Make a Payment Page</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement Information Pages (full-page and modal views)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Support Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>Shared global components including header, footer, modals, notifications=
, and error states</p></li>
<li>
<p>Personalised content rendering based on verified case data</p></li>
<li>
<p>Integration with backend systems for case data (e.g., Columbus) and paym=
ent gateway</p></li>
<li>
<p>Tracking of user interactions and engagement events across the journey</=
p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Customer App =E2=80=93 Landing Page Settings Module</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Landing Page Settings interface displaying content areas as structured c=
ards (e.g., Payment, Enforcement, Support)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Navigation from card view to detailed content editing view for each land=
ing page section</p></li>
<li>
<p>Content editing capability with:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Editable structured panels reflecting Landing Page layout</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ability to modify content directly as it appears to end users</p></li>
<li>
<p>Formatting options for content editing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ability to insert variables</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ability to create and manage hyperlinks</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Retention of page structure and layout during content editing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Mapping of panel names in the editor to corresponding Landing Page headi=
ngs</p></li>
<li>
<p>Logging of all changes within the audit trail</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Governance and Approval Workflow</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Three-step approval process:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Author (create/edit content)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reviewer (validate content)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Publisher (final release to production)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Integration with ticketing system for:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Change request creation</p></li>
<li>
<p>Tracking approvals and rejections</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement of role-based segregation within the workflow</p></li>
<li>
<p>Capture of approval decisions, comments, and timestamps</p></li>
<li>
<p>Publishing of approved content to production</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Audit, Tracking, and Reporting</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Audit logs capturing:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Content changes</p></li>
<li>
<p>User actions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Workflow status transitions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Approval and publishing records</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Tracking of workflow activities including:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Ticket creation</p></li>
<li>
<p>Approval/rejection events</p></li>
<li>
<p>Publishing confirmation</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Time and user stamp tracking for all actions</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Out of Scope</strong></p>
<p>The following items are explicitly excluded from this capability:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Development of a system-level permissions framework</p></li>
<li>
<p>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) system implementation</p></li>
<li>
<p>Automated approval or decision-making workflows</p></li>
<li>
<p>Redesign or modification of existing Landing Page UI/UX layouts created =
by external teams</p></li>
<li>
<p>Editing of structural components such as the timeline visualisation</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>Backend system changes related to case data management (e.g., Columbus s=
ystem redesign)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Live chat handling logic or integration within the support journey</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>Dispute handling, payment plan creation, or case modification functional=
ity</p></li>
<li>
<p>Passing personally identifiable information through external links or UR=
Ls</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p>This scope ensures clear separation between <strong>content management c=
apability</strong>, <strong>customer-facing functionality</strong>, and <st=
rong>underlying system responsibilities</strong>, enabling controlled and c=
ompliant implementation.</p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"2eb40c9c0e5d" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292101UsersandRol=
es"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc2302921=
01"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292101"></span></sp=
an>Users and Roles</h1>
<p>This capability involves multiple user types across both the customer-fa=
cing journey and the internal Customer App, with clearly defined responsibi=
lities to ensure controlled content management and governance.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Customer-Facing Users</strong></p>
<p><strong>Customer</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Primary end user of the Landing Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>Accesses the journey via SMS link and completes authentication</p></li>
<li>
<p>Interacts with:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Home / Timeline page</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment page</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement information</p></li>
<li>
<p>Support pages</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Performs key actions such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Viewing case details</p></li>
<li>
<p>Understanding enforcement stage</p></li>
<li>
<p>Making payments</p></li>
<li>
<p>Accessing support</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p>Customers do not have any content editing capability and only interact w=
ith published content.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Customer App Users (Internal Business Users)</strong></p>
<p>All internal users access the <strong>Customer App Landing Page Settings=
 module</strong> to manage and govern content displayed on Landing Pages. T=
hese users are assigned specific roles within the approval workflow.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Author</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Business user responsible for creating or editing Landing Page content</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Uses the Customer App editor to:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Access Landing Page settings</p></li>
<li>
<p>Edit content within structured panels</p></li>
<li>
<p>Apply formatting, insert variables, and configure hyperlinks</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Initiates change requests via the ticketing system</p></li>
<li>
<p>Responsible for ensuring initial accuracy of content updates</p></li>
<li>
<p>Cannot approve or publish their own changes</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Reviewer</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Business or compliance user responsible for validating changes</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reviews submitted content updates for:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Accuracy</p></li>
<li>
<p>Compliance with policies and regulations</p></li>
<li>
<p>Alignment with enforcement and business messaging</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Can:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Approve changes for publishing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reject changes with feedback for rework</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Must not be the same individual as the Author or Publisher for the same =
request</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Publisher</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Final approver responsible for releasing content to production</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reviews approved changes before publishing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensures readiness and correctness of content prior to go-live</p></li>
<li>
<p>Executes publishing action to make content visible on customer-facing La=
nding Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>Accountable for final sign-off</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Compliance Leads</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Oversight role across the entire process</p></li>
<li>
<p>Monitors:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Adherence to governance model</p></li>
<li>
<p>Audit logs and change history</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Supports compliance reviews and internal audits</p></li>
<li>
<p>Does not directly perform editing, reviewing, or publishing actions</p><=
/li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Role Governance Constraints</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>A single user must not perform multiple roles within the same request:</=
p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Author and Reviewer</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reviewer and Publisher</p></li>
<li>
<p>Author and Publisher</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>All content changes must pass through all three roles:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Author =E2=86=92 Reviewer =E2=86=92 Publisher</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Role assignments and actions must be fully traceable through audit logs<=
/p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"2552eead15a8" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292102LandingPage=
Overview(End-UserJourneySummary)"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=
=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292102"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=
=3D"_Toc230292102"></span></span>Landing Page Overview (End-User Journey Su=
mmary)</h1>
<p>The Landing Pages represent a structured, secure, and personalised digit=
al journey that enables customers to access case information, understand th=
eir enforcement status, and complete key actions such as making a payment o=
r seeking support. This journey is initiated through a controlled entry poi=
nt and progresses through a series of defined stages designed to ensure cla=
rity, security, and compliance.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Entry and Authentication</strong></p>
<p>The journey begins when a customer accesses the system via a generic SMS=
 link. Upon entry, the user is presented with a Sign-In / Identity Verifica=
tion page where they must provide required credentials (such as postcode an=
d other validation inputs). Authentication is enforced with controlled atte=
mpt limits, and access to any personal or case-related information is restr=
icted until verification is successfully completed.</p>
<p>If authentication fails, the system provides controlled retry attempts a=
nd recovery options. Upon exceeding the allowed attempts, the user is restr=
icted from further access and directed to recovery or support channels.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Case Retrieval and Personalisation</strong></p>
<p>Once authenticated, the system retrieves the customer=E2=80=99s case dat=
a from backend systems. This includes key attributes such as case reference=
, enforcement stage, outstanding balance, and applicable fees. This data dr=
ives all subsequent page behaviour, including content personalisation, time=
line positioning, and action prioritisation.</p>
<p>Personalisation is dynamically applied based on verified data, ensuring =
that all information displayed is accurate, relevant, and contextual to the=
 customer=E2=80=99s situation.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Home / Timeline Page (Primary Landing Page)</strong></p>
<p>The Home / Timeline page serves as the central point of the journey and =
the primary decision-making interface for the customer. This page provides:=
</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>A visual timeline representing the customer=E2=80=99s enforcement stage<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>A summary of the case, including balance and status</p></li>
<li>
<p>Contextual messaging explaining the current position and next steps</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>A clearly defined primary call-to-action (typically =E2=80=9CPay Now=E2=
=80=9D)</p></li>
</ul>
<p>The timeline simplifies complex backend enforcement stages into a clear,=
 structured visual representation to improve customer understanding and red=
uce confusion.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Customer Decision Paths</strong></p>
<p>From the Home / Timeline page, the user is guided into one of the follow=
ing paths:</p>
<p><strong>1. Payment Path (Primary Path)</strong></p>
<p>The user selects the primary call-to-action and is directed to the Payme=
nt page, where they can:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Review outstanding balance and fees</p></li>
<li>
<p>Confirm payment details</p></li>
<li>
<p>Proceed to a secure external payment gateway</p></li>
</ul>
<p>Upon successful payment, the system confirms the transaction and updates=
 the case status accordingly.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2. Enforcement Information Path</strong></p>
<p>Users may choose to view additional information about their enforcement =
stage. This provides:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Stage-specific explanations</p></li>
<li>
<p>Consequences of non-payment</p></li>
<li>
<p>Clear description of what happens next</p></li>
</ul>
<p>This path is designed to improve understanding and encourage informed de=
cision-making without causing confusion or escalation.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>3. Support Path</strong></p>
<p>Users can access support-related content which includes:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Frequently asked questions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Vulnerability support options</p></li>
<li>
<p>Complaint and assistance routes</p></li>
</ul>
<p>This path provides reassurance and assistance while maintaining alignmen=
t with the overall journey objectives.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Journey Outcomes</strong></p>
<p>The journey supports multiple outcomes:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Successful outcome:</strong> Payment completed and case updated<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Return path:</strong> User navigates back to the Home page or co=
ntinues the journey</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Exit path:</strong> User leaves the journey or transitions to of=
fline support channels</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Journey Design Principles</strong></p>
<p>The Landing Page journey is built on the following principles:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Security:</strong> No personal data is exposed prior to successf=
ul authentication</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Clarity:</strong> Complex information is simplified through visu=
al and structured presentation</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Guided Action:</strong> Primary actions are clearly highlighted =
to drive completion</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Compliance:</strong> Content and messaging follow regulatory and=
 policy requirements</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Continuity:</strong> The journey avoids dead ends, always provid=
ing a next actionable step</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"ac333c8d9e79" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292103CustomerApp=
=E2=80=93LandingPageSettingsOverview"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link=
" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292103"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link=
" id=3D"_Toc230292103"></span></span>Customer App =E2=80=93 Landing Page Se=
ttings Overview</h1>
<p>The Customer App Landing Page Settings module provides authorised busine=
ss users with the capability to manage, edit, review, and publish content t=
hat is displayed across all customer-facing Landing Pages. This module acts=
 as the central content management interface, enabling controlled updates w=
hile ensuring consistency, compliance, and auditability.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Access and Navigation</strong></p>
<p>When a user accesses the Landing Page Settings section within the Custom=
er App, they are presented with a structured interface consisting of visual=
ly distinct cards. Each card represents a major Landing Page content area, =
such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Make a Payment</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement</p></li>
<li>
<p>Support</p></li>
</ul>
<p>These cards serve as entry points for managing content associated with s=
pecific sections of the customer journey.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Content Editing Experience</strong></p>
<p>Upon selecting and editing a card, the user is navigated to a dedicated =
content editing view corresponding to that section. The editor is designed =
to mirror the structure and layout of the actual customer-facing Landing Pa=
ges, allowing users to view and modify content in the same format as it app=
ears to end users.</p>
<p>The content editing interface includes the following capabilities:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Direct content editing within structured panels</strong>, mainta=
ining alignment with Landing Page layout</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Panel-based organisation</strong>, where each panel represents a=
 distinct content block or section</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Panel names mapped to Landing Page headings</strong>, ensuring c=
larity and consistency between editor and live pages</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Preservation of layout and structure</strong>, preventing uninte=
nded changes to page design</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Content Authoring Capabilities</strong></p>
<p>Business users are able to manage content using the following features:<=
/p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Apply formatting to content (e.g., structured text presentation)</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>Insert variables to dynamically reflect case-specific or contextual info=
rmation</p></li>
<li>
<p>Create and configure hyperlinks within content</p></li>
</ul>
<p>These capabilities enable flexible yet controlled content management whi=
le ensuring the output remains consistent with the defined Landing Page exp=
erience.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Content Lifecycle and Workflow Integration</strong></p>
<p>All changes made within the editor are part of a controlled lifecycle al=
igned with the governance model. Users can:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Save changes within the editor</p></li>
<li>
<p>Submit changes for review through the defined approval process</p></li>
</ul>
<p>The workflow consists of:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Authoring</strong> =E2=80=93 content creation and editing</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Review</strong> =E2=80=93 validation of content for compliance a=
nd accuracy</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Publishing</strong> =E2=80=93 final approval and release to prod=
uction</p></li>
</ol>
<p>Users cannot directly publish content without completing the required re=
view and approval stages.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Audit and Traceability</strong></p>
<p>Every action within the Landing Page Settings module is tracked to ensur=
e full transparency and accountability. This includes:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Logging of all content changes</p></li>
<li>
<p>Recording user actions (create, edit, submit, approve, reject, publish)<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Capturing timestamps and user identifiers for each action</p></li>
<li>
<p>Maintaining an audit log that reflects the complete history of changes</=
p></li>
</ul>
<p>This ensures that all modifications to customer-facing content are trace=
able and compliant with governance requirements.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Design Principles</strong></p>
<p>The Customer App editor is designed with the following principles:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>What-you-see-is-what-you-edit approach</strong>, ensuring consis=
tency between editor and live pages</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Structured editing</strong>, preventing deviation from approved =
page layouts</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Controlled flexibility</strong>, allowing content updates withou=
t impacting system behaviour or layout</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Governance-first design</strong>, ensuring all changes pass thro=
ugh review and approval controls</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"78a955366627" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292104FunctionalR=
equirements"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_T=
oc230292104"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292104"></=
span></span>Functional Requirements</h1>
<p><strong>7.1 Landing Pages (Customer-Facing)</strong></p>
<p>The system shall provide a set of customer-facing Landing Pages that ena=
ble a secure, personalised, and structured journey from authentication to p=
ayment completion.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system shall display a Sign-In / ID&amp;V page as the entry point, r=
estricting access to case data until successful verification</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall retrieve and render case data dynamically post-authenti=
cation, including enforcement stage, balance, and fees</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall display a Home / Timeline page with a visual representa=
tion of the customer=E2=80=99s enforcement stage</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall present a primary Call-to-Action (CTA) to guide users t=
oward payment</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow navigation to the Payment page, Enforcement Infor=
mation pages, and Support pages from the Home page</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall display the Payment page with accurate case summary, ba=
lance, and applicable fees</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall enable redirection to a secure external payment gateway=
 for transaction processing</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall handle payment success and failure states and provide a=
ppropriate feedback to the user</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall display Enforcement Information pages with stage-specif=
ic explanations and consequences</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall display Support pages with structured assistance option=
s, including FAQs and escalation routes</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall ensure all pages are session-bound and accessible only =
after successful authentication</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall track all user interactions and key events across the L=
anding Page journey</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>7.2 Customer App =E2=80=93 Content Editor</strong></p>
<p>The system shall provide a Landing Page Settings module within the Custo=
mer App to enable business users to manage and control Landing Page content=
.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system shall display Landing Page content areas as structured cards =
(e.g., Payment, Enforcement, Support)</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow users to select and edit a specific card, navigat=
ing to a corresponding content editing screen</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall present content in a structured format that mirrors the=
 layout and appearance of the customer-facing Landing Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall organise content into panels, with each panel represent=
ing a section of the Landing Page</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall display panel names aligned with corresponding headings=
 in the Landing Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow users to edit content directly within panels with=
out altering the overall page structure</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall provide formatting options to modify content presentati=
on</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow insertion of variables within content</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow creation and configuration of hyperlinks within c=
ontent</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall preserve the visual structure and layout of Landing Pag=
es during editing</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow users to save content changes prior to submission=
</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall ensure that all content changes are captured and reflec=
ted in the audit log</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>7.3 Governance and Approval Workflow</strong></p>
<p>The system shall enforce a structured, business-led approval workflow go=
verning all content changes.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system shall support a three-step workflow: Author =E2=86=92 Reviewe=
r =E2=86=92 Publisher</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow Authors to create and submit content changes for =
review</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall enable integration with a ticketing system for managing=
 change requests</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow assignment of Author, Reviewer, and Publisher rol=
es per request</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall prevent a single user from performing multiple roles wi=
thin the same request</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow Reviewers to approve or reject submitted changes<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall require Reviewers to provide feedback when rejecting ch=
anges</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow only approved changes to proceed to the publishin=
g stage</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall allow Publishers to perform final review and publish co=
ntent to production</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall prevent publishing without prior approval</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall capture all workflow actions including submission, appr=
oval, rejection, and publishing</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system shall record timestamps and user identifiers for each workflo=
w stage</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"206325a9b6c5" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292105BusinessReq=
uirements(BR)"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-=
_Toc230292105"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292105">=
</span></span>Business Requirements (BR)</h1>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1800" data-layout=3D"default" class=3D"confluenc=
eTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#F5F5F5" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>BR ID</strong></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#F5F5F5" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Requirement</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR=E2=80=9101</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system must provide secure access to Landing Pages, ensuring no cust=
omer data is exposed prior to successful authentication</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR=E2=80=9102</p></td>
