<h1 local-id=3D"99adaf3c3c33" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292106BusinessRul=
es"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc2302921=
06"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292106"></span></sp=
an>Business Rules</h1>
<p>The following business rules govern the behaviour of both the customer-f=
acing Landing Pages and the Customer App Landing Page Settings module, ensu=
ring consistency, compliance, and controlled content management.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Customer-Facing Business Rules</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Customers must not be able to access any case or personal data prior to =
successful authentication</p></li>
<li>
<p>Access to Landing Pages must be restricted to verified sessions only</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>The system must display information for one case at a time within the La=
nding Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>In scenarios with multiple cases, a default case must be selected based =
on defined prioritisation logic (e.g., urgency)</p></li>
<li>
<p>All case-related data (balance, fees, enforcement stage) must match back=
end system values at all times</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement messaging must be accurate, factual, and compliant with appl=
icable policies</p></li>
<li>
<p>Timeline representation must reflect the mapped enforcement stage and mu=
st not be editable through the Customer App</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment actions must always be tied to the currently active case</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>Payment attempts must not restrict or lock the user out of the overall j=
ourney</p></li>
<li>
<p>All navigation paths must ensure no dead-end states, providing users wit=
h clear next actions</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Customer App =E2=80=93 Content Management Rules</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Business users must only be able to edit content within predefined struc=
tured panels</p></li>
<li>
<p>The layout and structural elements of Landing Pages must remain unchange=
d during content editing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Panel names within the editor must align with corresponding headings in =
the Landing Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>All content changes must be saved before being submitted for review</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>Content editing must support formatting, variable insertion, and hyperli=
nk configuration</p></li>
<li>
<p>All changes made within the editor must be logged in the audit trail wit=
h user and timestamp details</p></li>
<li>
<p>Content must reflect how it appears to end users, ensuring consistency b=
etween editor and live view</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Governance and Approval Rules</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>A single user must not perform multiple roles within the same request:</=
p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Author and Reviewer</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reviewer and Publisher</p></li>
<li>
<p>Author and Publisher</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Every content change must pass through all three stages:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Author</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reviewer</p></li>
<li>
<p>Publisher</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Content must not be published without:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Explicit approval from the Reviewer</p></li>
<li>
<p>Final sign-off from the Publisher</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Rejected changes:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Must be returned to the Author with clear feedback</p></li>
<li>
<p>Must not proceed further in the workflow until updated and resubmitted</=
p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Publishing actions must only be available after successful completion of=
 the review stage</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Audit and Compliance Rules</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All actions, including creation, editing, submission, approval, rejectio=
n, and publishing must be fully logged</p></li>
<li>
<p>Each action must include:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>User identifier</p></li>
<li>
<p>Timestamp</p></li>
<li>
<p>Action performed</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Audit logs must be immutable and available for internal audit and compli=
ance review</p></li>
<li>
<p>Content updates must not bypass the defined governance workflow</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"9799788180b0" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292107Personalisa=
tionLogic"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc=
230292107"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292107"></sp=
an></span>Personalisation Logic</h1>
<p>Personalisation across the Landing Pages is driven entirely by verified =
case data retrieved post-authentication and system-defined contextual facto=
rs. The logic ensures that all customer-facing content remains accurate, re=
levant, and aligned with the customer=E2=80=99s current case status while m=
aintaining strict control over data exposure and content consistency.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Customer-Facing Personalisation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Personalisation is applied <strong>only after successful authentication<=
/strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>No personal or case-related data is displayed prior to verification</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>Personalised elements include:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Customer-specific greeting (where applicable)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Case reference and associated details</p></li>
<li>
<p>Debt type</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement stage</p></li>
<li>
<p>Outstanding balance and applicable fees</p></li>
<li>
<p>Time-sensitive indicators (e.g., countdowns where applicable)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The system must dynamically adapt page content based on:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The currently selected case</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement stage progression</p></li>
<li>
<p>Case status and conditions (e.g., active, on hold)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Single-case versus multi-case scenarios</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>In multi-case scenarios:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must default to a selected case based on defined prioritisati=
on logic</p></li>
<li>
<p>Users must be able to switch between cases where applicable</p></li>
<li>
<p>All displayed content must refresh dynamically based on the selected cas=
e</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement messaging, urgency indicators, and call-to-action (CTA) cont=
ent must adapt based on:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Stage progression (e.g., pre-compliance, compliance, enforcement)</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p>Severity of enforcement position</p></li>
<li>
<p>Applicable fees and consequences</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Personalisation must be rendered dynamically at runtime and must not be =
stored client-side</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Customer App Content Personalisation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Customer App does not directly control personalisation logic but ena=
bles the management of content that supports personalised rendering</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>Business users can:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Define and edit content templates that include placeholders or variables=
</p></li>
<li>
<p>Insert variables into content which will be resolved dynamically at runt=
ime based on case data</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Variables inserted through the editor must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Resolve to appropriate values during runtime based on backend data</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>Maintain consistency with system-defined personalisation logic</p></li>
<li>
<p>Not expose sensitive data prior to authentication</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Content updated via the Customer App must remain compatible with:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Existing personalisation rules</p></li>
<li>
<p>Case-based rendering logic</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement stage-based messaging</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Governance of Personalised Content</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All updates to content that influences personalisation must follow the d=
efined approval workflow:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Author =E2=86=92 Reviewer =E2=86=92 Publisher</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Personalisation-related updates must be:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Reviewed for accuracy and correctness of variable usage</p></li>
<li>
<p>Validated for compliance with regulatory and policy requirements</p></li=
>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>No personalised messaging or variable usage may be published without app=
roval</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Personalisation Constraints</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Personalisation must not:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Override system-driven data such as balance, fees, or enforcement stage<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Alter structural components such as the timeline</p></li>
<li>
<p>Introduce inconsistencies between displayed content and backend data</p>=
</li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>All personalised outputs must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Reflect real-time system data</p></li>
<li>
<p>Remain consistent across all Landing Pages and related components</p></l=
i>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"0bccb3ec7e8a" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292108BusinessPro=
cess/Workflow"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-=
_Toc230292108"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292108">=
</span></span>Business Process / Workflow</h1>
<p>The solution follows a structured, end-to-end workflow covering both the=
 <strong>customer-facing journey</strong> and the <strong>internal Customer=
 App content management and governance process</strong>. This ensures a sea=
mless customer experience while maintaining strict control over content cha=
nges.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1. Customer Journey Workflow</strong></p>
<p><strong>1.1 Entry</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Customer receives an SMS containing a generic link</p></li>
<li>
<p>Customer clicks the link and is directed to the Sign-In / ID&amp;V page<=
/p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1.2 Authentication</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Customer enters required verification details</p></li>
<li>
<p>System validates input against backend system</p></li>
<li>
<p>Outcomes:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Success:</strong> Secure session is created =E2=86=92 proceed to=
 case retrieval</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Failure:</strong> Remaining attempts are reduced</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Maximum attempts reached:</strong> Customer is redirected to rec=
overy/support options</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1.3 Case Retrieval</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>System retrieves all active cases from backend systems</p></li>
<li>
<p>Data includes:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Case reference</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement stage</p></li>
<li>
<p>Balance and fees</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>A default case is selected for display</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1.4 Home / Timeline Page</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Timeline is rendered based on enforcement stage</p></li>
<li>
<p>Case summary and personalised content are displayed</p></li>
<li>
<p>Primary CTA (e.g., =E2=80=9CPay Now=E2=80=9D) is presented</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1.5 Customer Decision Paths</strong></p>
<p>From the Home page, the customer can choose:</p>
<p><strong>a. Payment Path</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Customer selects =E2=80=9CPay Now=E2=80=9D</p></li>
<li>
<p>System loads Payment page with case details</p></li>
<li>
<p>Customer proceeds to secure payment gateway</p></li>
<li>
<p>Outcomes:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Success:</strong> Payment confirmed and case updated</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Failure:</strong> Error displayed, retry allowed</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>b. Enforcement Information Path</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Customer accesses stage-specific explanation</p></li>
<li>
<p>System displays:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Current stage</p></li>
<li>
<p>Consequences</p></li>
<li>
<p>Next steps</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Customer can:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Proceed to payment</p></li>
<li>
<p>Return to Home page</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>c. Support Path</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Customer accesses support options</p></li>
<li>
<p>System displays:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>FAQs</p></li>
<li>
<p>Vulnerability options</p></li>
<li>
<p>Complaint forms</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Customer can:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Submit request via external forms</p></li>
<li>
<p>Return to journey</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1.6 Journey Outcomes</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Successful outcome:</strong> Payment completed</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Return path:</strong> Customer navigates back within journey</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Exit path:</strong> Customer leaves or moves to offline support =
channels</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2. Customer App Content Management Workflow</strong></p>
<p><strong>2.1 Access Landing Page Settings</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Business user logs into Customer App</p></li>
<li>
<p>Navigates to Landing Page Settings</p></li>
<li>
<p>System displays content cards (e.g., Payment, Enforcement, Support)</p><=
/li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2.2 Content Editing (Author Stage)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>User selects a card and opens content editor</p></li>
<li>
<p>System displays structured panels reflecting Landing Page layout</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>User performs:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Content updates</p></li>
<li>
<p>Formatting changes</p></li>
<li>
<p>Variable insertion</p></li>
<li>
<p>Hyperlink creation</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>User saves the changes</p></li>
<li>
<p>User submits changes for review</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2.3 Review Stage (Reviewer)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Reviewer receives change request via ticketing system</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reviewer validates:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Accuracy</p></li>
<li>
<p>Compliance</p></li>
<li>
<p>Policy alignment</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Outcomes:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Approve:</strong> Moves to Publisher stage</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Reject:</strong> Returned to Author with feedback</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2.4 Publishing Stage (Publisher)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Publisher reviews approved content</p></li>
<li>
<p>Performs final validation</p></li>
<li>
<p>Publishes content to production</p></li>
<li>
<p>Content becomes visible on customer-facing Landing Pages</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>3. Audit and Tracking Workflow</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Each stage in the process is logged:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Content creation and edits</p></li>
<li>
<p>Submission for review</p></li>
<li>
<p>Approval / rejection actions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Publishing actions</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>System captures:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>User ID</p></li>
<li>
<p>Timestamp</p></li>
<li>
<p>Action performed</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Audit logs support:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Compliance review</p></li>
<li>
<p>Internal audits</p></li>
<li>
<p>Traceability of all changes</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>4. Governance Workflow Summary</strong></p>
<p>Author =E2=86=92 Edit &amp; Submit</p>
<p>=E2=86=93</p>
<p>Reviewer =E2=86=92 Approve / Reject</p>
<p>=E2=86=93</p>
<p>Publisher =E2=86=92 Final Approval &amp; Publish</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>No stage can be skipped</p></li>
<li>
<p>Role segregation enforced</p></li>
<li>
<p>Publishing only possible after approval</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>5. End-to-End Integration Flow</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Customer App content updates =E2=86=92 Approved =E2=86=92 Published</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>Published content =E2=86=92 Rendered in Landing Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>Landing Pages =E2=86=92 Driven by real-time backend data + managed conte=
nt</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"58432140d527" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292109Tracking&am=
p;ReportingRequirements"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLa=
ndingPage-_Toc230292109"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc2=
30292109"></span></span>Tracking &amp; Reporting Requirements</h1>
<p>The system must implement comprehensive tracking and reporting capabilit=
ies across both the <strong>customer-facing Landing Pages</strong> and the =
<strong>Customer App content management workflow</strong> to ensure full vi=
sibility, performance monitoring, and audit compliance.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1. Customer Journey Tracking</strong></p>
<p>The system must track all key user interactions across the Landing Pages=
 to enable behavioural analysis, conversion monitoring, and performance opt=
imisation.</p>
<p><strong>Tracked Events</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Page load events for all Landing Pages</p></li>
<li>
<p>Authentication attempts (success and failure)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Navigation between pages (Home, Payment, Enforcement, Support)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Timeline interactions (hover, tap, selection)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Case selection and switching (for multi-case scenarios)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Primary CTA clicks (e.g., =E2=80=9CPay Now=E2=80=9D)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Secondary CTA clicks (e.g., support links, informational links)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment journey events:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Payment initiation</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment method selection</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment submission</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment success</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment failure</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Captured Attributes</strong></p>
<p>Each tracked event must include:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Case reference</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement stage</p></li>
<li>
<p>Debt type (where applicable)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Multi-case indicator (true/false)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Page identifier</p></li>
<li>
<p>Timestamp</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Purpose</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Analyse user behaviour and drop-off points within the journey</p></li>
<li>
<p>Measure payment conversion rates</p></li>
<li>
<p>Identify friction points in authentication and payment flows</p></li>
<li>
<p>Support continuous optimisation of the Landing Page experience</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2. Customer App Tracking (Content Management)</strong></p>
<p>The system must track all activities performed within the Customer App L=
anding Page Settings module to ensure traceability and governance.</p>
<p><strong>Tracked Actions</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Access to Landing Page Settings module</p></li>
<li>
<p>Selection of content cards (e.g., Payment, Enforcement, Support)</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>Content edits within panels</p></li>
<li>
<p>Save actions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Submission for review</p></li>
<li>
<p>Approval actions by Reviewer</p></li>
<li>
<p>Rejection actions with feedback</p></li>
<li>
<p>Publishing actions by Publisher</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Captured Attributes</strong></p>
<p>Each activity must capture:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>User identifier (Author, Reviewer, Publisher)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Action performed</p></li>
<li>
<p>Affected content section</p></li>
<li>
<p>Timestamp</p></li>
<li>
<p>Status of request (pending, approved, rejected, published)</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Purpose</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Monitor content management activity</p></li>
<li>
<p>Track user actions for audit and governance</p></li>
<li>
<p>Identify bottlenecks in approval workflow</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>3. Governance and Audit Tracking</strong></p>
<p>The system must maintain a complete and immutable audit trail for all co=
ntent changes and workflow transitions.</p>
<p><strong>Audit Log Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Record all content modifications, including before and after states</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>Capture all workflow transitions:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Created</p></li>
<li>
<p>Submitted</p></li>
<li>
<p>Approved</p></li>
<li>
<p>Rejected</p></li>
<li>
<p>Published</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Store user and timestamp details for each action</p></li>
<li>
<p>Maintain association between content changes and related ticket/request<=
/p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Purpose</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Support internal and external audits</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure compliance with governance policies</p></li>
<li>
<p>Provide full traceability of all content changes</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>4. Reporting Requirements</strong></p>
<p>The system must support reporting capabilities to provide insights into =
both customer behaviour and internal operational efficiency.</p>
<p><strong>Customer Journey Reports</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Page-level engagement metrics</p></li>
<li>
<p>Drop-off analysis across journey stages</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment conversion rates</p></li>
<li>
<p>Authentication success and failure rates</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Content Management Reports</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Volume of content changes over time</p></li>
<li>
<p>Approval and rejection rates</p></li>
<li>
<p>Time taken for each workflow stage (Author =E2=86=92 Reviewer =E2=86=92 =
Publisher)</p></li>
<li>
<p>User activity reports by role</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>5. Data Handling and Constraints</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All tracking data must be captured securely and aligned with data protec=
tion policies</p></li>
<li>
<p>No sensitive personal data should be exposed unnecessarily in reporting =
outputs</p></li>
<li>
<p>Tracking mechanisms must not impact page performance or user experience<=
/p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"3598bf1e3144" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292110Configurati=
onRequirements"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage=
-_Toc230292110"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292110"=
></span></span>Configuration Requirements</h1>
<p>The system must support configurable elements across both the <strong>cu=
stomer-facing Landing Pages</strong> and the <strong>Customer App Landing P=
age Settings module</strong> to ensure flexibility, scalability, and ease o=
f maintenance without requiring code-level changes.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1. Customer-Facing Configuration Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Landing Page content must be configurable through the Customer App, allo=
wing updates without system deployment</p></li>
<li>
<p>Content displayed across all Landing Pages must be dynamically driven ba=
sed on configured values and backend data</p></li>
<li>
<p>The following elements must be configurable:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Text content (headings, descriptions, messages)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Call-to-Action (CTA) labels and messaging</p></li>
<li>
<p>Support-related content and links</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement-related messaging and explanatory content</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment-related messaging and instructions</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Threshold-based elements must be configurable where applicable:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Time-sensitive messaging triggers</p></li>
<li>
<p>Countdown thresholds (if applicable to enforcement stages)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>All configurable content must be centrally managed through the Customer =
App to ensure consistency across pages</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2. Customer App Configuration Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Landing Page Settings module must allow configuration of:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Content mapped to different Landing Page sections (e.g., Payment, Enforc=
ement, Support)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Structured panels aligned to Landing Page layout and headings</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The system must support:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Configuration of variables that can be inserted into content</p></li>
<li>
<p>Configuration of hyperlink destinations used within content</p></li>
<li>
<p>Configuration of formatting options available within the editor</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Panel structures and layout definitions must be predefined and remain co=
nsistent across environments</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system must allow configuration of:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Visibility of content sections (where applicable)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Contextual content alignment with specific Landing Page areas</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>3. Governance and Workflow Configuration</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The approval workflow must be configurable within the existing ticketing=
 system, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Workflow stages (Author, Reviewer, Publisher)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Status transitions (Pending, Approved, Rejected, Published)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The system must allow configuration of:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Role definitions (Author, Reviewer, Publisher)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Notification triggers (e.g., email alerts for submission, approval, reje=
ction)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Routing of requests between roles</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>4. Integration Configuration</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Integration endpoints must be configurable for:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Backend case data system (e.g., Columbus)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment gateway redirection</p></li>
<li>
<p>External support forms</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>URLs used within Landing Pages must be configurable and centrally mainta=
ined</p></li>
<li>
<p>Any environment-specific configurations (e.g., test vs production endpoi=
nts) must be manageable without code changes</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>5. Audit and Tracking Configuration</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must allow configuration of:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Audit logging parameters</p></li>
<li>
<p>Tracking event definitions (where applicable)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Retention of audit and tracking data</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>6. Constraints</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Structural components such as the timeline visualisation must not be con=
figurable through the Customer App</p></li>
<li>
<p>Configuration must not allow changes that impact system-driven logic suc=
h as:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Enforcement stage mapping</p></li>
<li>
<p>Case data retrieval</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment processing logic</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>All configuration changes must be subject to the defined governance and =
approval workflow before becoming active</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"9baf71b1afcc" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292111Link&amp;Ac=
cessRequirements"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPa=
ge-_Toc230292111"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc23029211=
1"></span></span>Link &amp; Access Requirements</h1>
<p>The system must enforce controlled, secure, and appropriate access mecha=
nisms for both <strong>customer-facing Landing Pages</strong> and the <stro=
ng>Customer App Landing Page Settings module</strong>, ensuring that all ac=
cess points, navigation paths, and external links comply with security, pri=
vacy, and governance requirements.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1. Customer-Facing Access Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All Landing Pages must be accessible <strong>only after successful user =
authentication</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>The system must ensure that:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>No unauthorised or unauthenticated access to case data is possible</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>All pages are session-bound and tied to a verified user session</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Session handling must ensure:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Access continuity across the customer journey</p></li>
<li>
<p>Automatic restriction of access once the session is terminated or expire=
d</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Direct URL access to internal pages (e.g., Payment, Enforcement, Support=
) must not bypass authentication or session validation</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2. URL and Navigation Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All Landing Page URLs must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Be secure and not expose any personally identifiable information (PII)</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Avoid embedding customer-specific identifiers (e.g., case reference, pos=
tcode)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Navigation between pages must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Be handled internally within the secured session</p></li>
<li>
<p>Preserve context (e.g., selected case, enforcement stage)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>External links (e.g., support forms, payment gateway) must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Open in a controlled manner (same tab or new tab as defined by design)</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Not expose sensitive session or customer data via URL parameters</p></li=
>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>3. Payment Gateway Access</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must allow access to the payment gateway <strong>only from an=
 authenticated session</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>Redirection to the payment gateway must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Be secure and validated</p></li>
<li>
<p>Include only necessary, non-sensitive transaction data</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Return from the payment gateway must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Be validated against the originating session</p></li>
<li>
<p>Route the user back to the appropriate state within the journey (success=
 or failure)</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>4. Support and External Links</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Links to external support forms (e.g., complaints, vulnerability, =E2=80=
=9CNot at this address=E2=80=9D) must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Open securely in a new tab or controlled context</p></li>
<li>
<p>Not pass any sensitive personal or case data via URL</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Upon returning from external links:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The user=E2=80=99s session context should be preserved where applicable<=
/p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>5. Customer App Access Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Landing Page Settings module must be accessible <strong>only to auth=
orised internal business users</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>Access must be restricted to:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Users assigned appropriate roles (Author, Reviewer, Publisher)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The system must ensure:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>No customer-facing exposure of internal tools or content editor</p></li>
<li>
<p>Secure authentication and access to the Customer App</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Actions performed within the Customer App must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Be linked to authenticated user identities</p></li>
<li>
<p>Be logged for audit and traceability</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>6. Governance and Workflow Access</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Access to workflow actions must be role-based:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Only Authors can create and submit changes</p></li>
<li>
<p>Only Reviewers can approve or reject changes</p></li>
<li>
<p>Only Publishers can publish approved content</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The system must enforce:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Users cannot perform multiple roles within the same request</p></li>
<li>
<p>Workflow actions are accessible only at the appropriate stage</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>7. Security and Data Protection Constraints</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>No Personally Identifiable Information (PII) must be:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Exposed in URLs</p></li>
<li>
<p>Passed through external links</p></li>
<li>
<p>Stored client-side beyond session requirements</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>All links and access points must comply with:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Applicable data protection and security standards</p></li>
<li>
<p>Internal security and governance policies</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"17af2bdeaa7a" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292112Non-Functio=
nalRequirements"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPag=
e-_Toc230292112"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292112=
"></span></span>Non-Functional Requirements</h1>
<p>The system must meet defined non-functional requirements to ensure perfo=
rmance, scalability, security, accessibility, and reliability across both t=
he <strong>customer-facing Landing Pages</strong> and the <strong>Customer =
App Landing Page Settings module</strong>.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1. Performance Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All Landing Pages must load within <strong>2 seconds under standard oper=
ating conditions</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>Timeline rendering and dynamic data loading must be <strong>near-instant=
aneous post-authentication</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>Customer App editor screens must load without noticeable delay, ensuring=
 a smooth editing experience</p></li>
<li>
<p>Content updates and publishing actions must be executed without impactin=
g system responsiveness</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2. Availability and Reliability</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must maintain <strong>high availability</strong> during opera=
tional hours, ensuring uninterrupted access for customers and business user=
s</p></li>
<li>
<p>Integration points (e.g., backend data systems, payment gateway, ticketi=
ng system) must be reliable and monitored</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system must handle partial failures gracefully, ensuring:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Clear error messaging</p></li>
<li>
<p>No data corruption or inconsistent states</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Published content must be consistently available across all Landing Page=
s without delay</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>3. Security Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All data exchanges must be <strong>secure and encrypted</strong></p></li=
>
<li>
<p>Access to customer-facing pages must be restricted to <strong>authentica=
ted sessions only</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>Customer App access must be restricted to <strong>authorised business us=
ers</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>No sensitive data must be:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Exposed before authentication</p></li>
<li>
<p>Stored unnecessarily on the client side</p></li>
<li>
<p>Passed through URLs or external links</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The system must comply with applicable <strong>data protection and secur=
ity standards</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>4. Accessibility Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All customer-facing Landing Pages must adhere to <strong>WCAG 2.1 / 2.2 =
AA compliance standards</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p>Pages must be:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Fully navigable via keyboard</p></li>
<li>
<p>Compatible with screen readers</p></li>
<li>
<p>Designed with sufficient colour contrast and readable typography</p></li=
>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Customer App interfaces must also follow accessibility best practices to=
 ensure usability for all business users</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>5. Scalability Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must support increasing volumes of:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Customer traffic</p></li>
<li>
<p>Content updates</p></li>
<li>
<p>Concurrent users on the Customer App</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The architecture must allow for <strong>scaling without degradation of p=
erformance</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>6. Usability Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Landing Pages must follow a <strong>clear, intuitive design</strong> all=
owing users to easily understand their case and next steps</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Customer App editor must provide a <strong>structured and easy-to-us=
e interface</strong> that reflects the end-user view</p></li>
<li>
<p>Content editing must be straightforward, ensuring minimal training is re=
quired for business users</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>7. Maintainability Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Content updates must be manageable without requiring system deployment</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Configuration changes must be applied without impacting live system stab=
ility</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system must support easy maintenance of:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Content structures</p></li>
<li>
<p>Workflow configurations</p></li>
<li>
<p>Integration endpoints</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>8. Audit and Logging Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must maintain <strong>complete audit logs</strong> for all ac=
tions within the Customer App</p></li>
<li>
<p>Logs must be:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Accurate</p></li>
<li>
<p>Time-stamped</p></li>
<li>
<p>User-specific</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Audit data must be retained as per organisational and regulatory policie=
s</p></li>
<li>
<p>Logging mechanisms must not impact system performance</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>9. Compatibility and Responsiveness</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Landing Pages must be fully <strong>responsive across devices</strong>:<=
/p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Desktop</p></li>
<li>
<p>Tablet</p></li>
<li>
<p>Mobile</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The system must support all major modern browsers</p></li>
<li>
<p>Customer App interfaces must also adapt across supported resolutions and=
 devices</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>10. Compliance Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must adhere to:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Data protection regulations (e.g., GDPR principles where applicable)</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>Industry standards related to payment processing (e.g., PCI-DSS complian=
ce via payment gateway)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Internal compliance and governance policies</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"63128039ddd3" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292113UI/UXBehavi=
our(CustomerAppEditor)"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLan=
dingPage-_Toc230292113"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc23=
0292113"></span></span>UI / UX Behaviour (Customer App Editor)</h1>
<p>The Customer App Landing Page Settings module must provide a structured,=
 intuitive, and controlled user interface that enables business users to ma=
nage Landing Page content effectively while preserving the integrity of the=
 end-user experience.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1. Landing Page Settings Overview Screen</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must display Landing Page sections as <strong>individual card=
s</strong>, representing key areas such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Make a Payment</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement</p></li>
<li>
<p>Support</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Each card must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Clearly represent a distinct Landing Page section</p></li>
<li>
<p>Provide a visual entry point to manage corresponding content</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Selecting a card must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Navigate the user to the detailed content editing interface for that sec=
tion</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2. Content Editing Interface</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must present a <strong>structured editing view</strong> that =
mirrors the layout and appearance of the corresponding customer-facing Land=
ing Page</p></li>
<li>
<p>Content must be organised into <strong>panels</strong>, where:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Each panel represents a specific section or content block</p></li>
<li>
<p>Panel names must match the headings displayed on the Landing Pages</p></=
li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The editor must follow a <strong>What-You-See-Is-What-You-Edit (WYSIWYE)=
</strong> approach, ensuring:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Visual alignment between editor and live page</p></li>
<li>
<p>Clear understanding of how content will appear to end users</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>3. Content Editing Capabilities</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must allow users to:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Edit text content directly within panels</p></li>
<li>
<p>Apply formatting to content (e.g., structured text presentation)</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>Insert variables to support dynamic content rendering</p></li>
<li>
<p>Create and manage hyperlinks within content</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The system must ensure:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The structural layout of the page is preserved at all times</p></li>
<li>
<p>Users cannot alter non-editable components such as layout or timeline el=
ements</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>4. Interaction Behaviour</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must allow users to:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Save changes during editing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Submit content for review after saving</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The UI must clearly indicate:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Current state of the content (e.g., edited, submitted)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Available actions based on workflow stage</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Navigation within the editor must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Allow users to move between panels easily</p></li>
<li>
<p>Maintain context without losing unsaved changes</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>5. Workflow Visibility</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The interface must provide clear visual indicators of workflow status, i=
ncluding:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Pending</p></li>
<li>
<p>Approved</p></li>
<li>
<p>Rejected</p></li>
<li>
<p>Published</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Users must be able to:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Identify the current stage of a content change</p></li>
<li>
<p>View feedback in case of rejection</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p>]</p>
<p><strong>6. Audit Visibility</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system must provide visibility into audit-related information, inclu=
ding:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Changes made to content</p></li>
<li>
<p>User who performed the change</p></li>
<li>
<p>Timestamp of change</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Audit information may be displayed within:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>A dedicated audit log view</p></li>
<li>
<p>Or as contextual information within the editor</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>7. Usability and Accessibility</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The editor must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Be intuitive and require minimal training for business users</p></li>
<li>
<p>Provide clear labelling of panels and actions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Maintain consistency across all sections</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The interface must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Support responsive behaviour across screen sizes</p></li>
<li>
<p>Follow accessibility best practices where applicable</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>8. Constraints</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Users must not be able to:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Modify structural elements of the Landing Page</p></li>
<li>
<p>Change layout or positioning of components</p></li>
<li>
<p>Edit system-driven elements such as timeline visualisation</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>All editing actions must:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Be part of the defined governance workflow</p></li>
<li>
<p>Be logged for audit and traceability</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"da42137756c0" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_Toc230292114Risks&amp;D=
ependencies"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BRDLandingPage-_T=
oc230292114"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc230292114"></=
span></span>Risks &amp; Dependencies</h1>
<p>The successful implementation and operation of the Landing Pages and Cus=
tomer App Landing Page Settings module are dependent on multiple systems, p=
rocesses, and design considerations. The following risks and dependencies h=
ave been identified.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1. Risks</strong></p>
<p><strong>1.1 Customer Journey Risks</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>user drop-off during authentication</strong> due to fail=
ed attempts or friction in the sign-in process</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>user abandonment</strong> if enforcement messaging is pe=
rceived as too aggressive or unclear</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>payment drop-off</strong> during redirection to the exte=
rnal payment gateway</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>confusion in multi-case scenarios</strong> if case prior=
itisation and selection are not clearly understood by users</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1.2 Content and UX Risks</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>incorrect or misleading content</strong> being published=
 if not properly reviewed</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>inconsistent messaging</strong> across Landing Pages if =
content updates are not centrally controlled</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>layout inconsistency</strong> if editing controls are no=
t strictly enforced</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>content complexity increasing</strong>, reducing clarity=
 for end users</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1.3 Governance and Process Risks</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>delays in content publishing</strong> due to dependency =
on Author =E2=86=92 Reviewer =E2=86=92 Publisher workflow</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>workflow bottlenecks</strong> if roles are not adequatel=
y resourced</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>process bypass</strong> if governance controls are not s=
trictly enforced</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>human error</strong> during manual approval processes</p=
></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1.4 Technical Risks</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>dependency on external systems</strong> (e.g., backend c=
ase system, payment gateway, ticketing system) affecting availability and p=
erformance</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>data inconsistency</strong> if backend system data is de=
layed or inaccurate</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>integration failures</strong> between systems impacting =
user journey or content publishing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>performance degradation</strong> under high traffic cond=
itions</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>1.5 Compliance and Security Risks</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>data exposure</strong> if access controls and session ma=
nagement are not properly enforced</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>non-compliance</strong> due to incorrect enforcement mes=
saging or content updates</p></li>
<li>
<p>Risk of <strong>incomplete audit trails</strong> affecting compliance an=
d audit requirements</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2. Dependencies</strong></p>
<p><strong>2.1 System Dependencies</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Backend case management system (e.g., Columbus) for:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Case data retrieval</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enforcement stage and status</p></li>
<li>
<p>Balance and fee information</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Payment gateway provider for:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Secure payment processing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Transaction confirmation and status updates</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Ticketing system for:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Managing content change requests</p></li>
<li>
<p>Supporting approval workflow (Author, Reviewer, Publisher)</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2.2 Content and Governance Dependencies</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Availability and definition of:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Business users (Authors, Reviewers, Publishers)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Compliance teams for review and oversight</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Timely review and approval of content updates</p></li>
<li>
<p>Adherence to governance processes and role segregation</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2.3 Design and UX Dependencies</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Finalised Landing Page designs provided by external/offshore teams</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>Alignment between Customer App editor layout and Landing Page structure<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Availability of approved content templates and messaging guidelines</p><=
/li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2.4 Operational Dependencies</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Availability of resources to manage content updates and workflow stages<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Coordination between business, compliance, and technical teams</p></li>
<li>
<p>Monitoring and support for system health, performance, and incidents</p>=
</li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>2.5 Data and Integration Dependencies</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Accuracy and availability of real-time case data</p></li>
<li>
<p>Stability and performance of API integrations</p></li>
<li>
<p>Secure handling of data during external interactions (e.g., payment gate=
way, support forms)</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>3. Mitigation Considerations</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"17851c0bc2d3">
<li>
<p>Enforce strict governance rules and audit logging for all content change=
s</p></li>
<li>
<p>Provide clear UI feedback and guidance to reduce user confusion and erro=
r</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensure robust integration monitoring and fallback mechanisms</p></li>
<li>
<p>Define operational SLAs for content approval and publishing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d1bedd073fe7">
<p local-id=3D"78a819c09739">Regularly review content and workflows for com=
pliance and effectiveness</p></li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
